<title>UK: Argentina's BICE sets $100 million four-year bond.</title>
<headline>Argentina's BICE sets $100 million four-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager ING Barings.</p>
<p> BORROWER   BANCO DE INVERSIONES E COMMERCIO EXTERIOR SA (BICE)</p>
<p> GUARANTOR  ARGENTINA</p>
<p> AMT    $100 MLN	COUPON     9.375     MATURITY    27.DEC.00</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  99.755    PAY DATE    27.DEC.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  45 BP     REOFFER    99.755    SPREAD	+338 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	=	   LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    =SEMI ANN</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  =	   DENOMS (K) 10-100    SALE LIMS US/UK/JP/AG</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    NEW YORK  HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    20 BP     SELL CONC  25 BP     PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 5.50 PCT 2000 U.S. TREASURY. -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
